<BaseLayout title="Method" description="How Vale Lab investigates emerging technology.">
  <article>
    <p class="eyebrow">Public research method</p>
    <h1>Useful, skeptical, auditable.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Vale Lab follows a qualitative method for fast but defensible technology investigations. It is not a substitute for formal peer review.</p>
    <h2>How an investigation moves</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Frame one precise question and connect it to a Vale project or decision.</li>
      <li>Build a source stack with primary papers, technical documentation, repositories, and institutional work first.</li>
      <li>Record an evidence table, including confidence and caveats for major claims.</li>
      <li>Steelman the strongest skeptical interpretation and distinguish demonstrated results from inference and speculation.</li>
      <li>Assess maturity, lawful practical reuse, and the smallest safe experiment that could change our view.</li>
      <li>Prepare a research packet before a human reviews a draft for publication.</li>
    </ol>
    <h2>Publication standard</h2>
    <p>Substantive external claims require inspectable sources. We identify uncertainty, do not launder citations, and label early work honestly. Automation can assist discovery and drafting; a human editor approves what is published.</p>
    <p><a href="https://github.com/adamolson11/myFuturisticTechBlog/blob/main/docs/RESEARCH_METHOD.md">Read the full research method</a> and <a href="https://github.com/adamolson11/myFuturisticTechBlog/blob/main/docs/SOURCE_AND_CITATION_POLICY.md">source and citation policy</a>.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
